   "he": "גְּמָ׳ מְנָלַן דְּפִשְׁתָּן אִיקְּרִי ״עֵץ״? אָמַר מָר זוּטְרָא: דְּאָמַר קְרָא ״וְהִיא הֶעֱלָתַם הַגָּגָה וַתִּטְמְנֵם בְּפִשְׁתֵּי הָעֵץ״.",
   "en": "«GEMARA:» The mishna mentioned flax as a material that comes from a tree. The Gemara asks: «From where do we» derive that «flax is called a tree?» Based on appearance, it does not resemble a tree at all. «Mar Zutra said:» It is derived from that which the «verse said: “And she had taken them up to the roof and hidden them under the trees of flax”» (Joshua 2:6)."
  }
